  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 607 AM EDT Sat Aug 22 2026\n\nA cold front extending from low pressure over MI is draped across \nour CWA from Three Rivers, MI down into White County, IN. Showers \nand storms have formed along this boundary, with one stronger storm \nnear Wabash/Whitley/Kosciusko County lines as of this writing. The \nfront will drift eastward through the afternoon, with a second \nshortwave/trough moving in behind it. This will lead to additional \nstorms in NW OH this afternoon/eve as we destabilize. Otherwise, \nhighs will be in the 70s, low 80s with gusty northwest winds. \n\nThe surface low/low aloft sinks into southern Ontario by Sun Eve/Mon \nAm, with our area in persistent northwest flow. There are low \nchances for showers and storms (20-35 percent) on Sunday before we \nare trapped beneath the upper level ridge. Dry conditions persist \ninto Wednesday afternoon before another broad trough encompasses the \nupper Great Lakes Wed eve into next Saturday.\n\nNorthwest flow of 15-20 knots with gusts up to around 25 knots on \nLake MI through the next couple of days will build waves to 3 to 6 \nfeet today into Sunday, with dangerous currents possible. Maintained \nthe going beach hazards statement, and extended the small craft \nadvisory.  There may be a lull in the wave/wind activity later \ntonight before waves climb up again on Sunday.",
